# Mend Unified Agent configuration for the symfony real-world probe.
#
# Read only by the Dev Platform envs (ghc_*_dp): DP does not read .whitesource,
# so the framework pushes this file as the tenant's UA config. .whitesource stays
# on configMode AUTO, so ghc_dev / ghc_staging / ghe keep ignoring this file and
# their currently-green runs are unaffected.
#
# WHY runPreStep=false. DP defaults php.runPreStep to TRUE and attempts a real
# `composer update`. symfony is a monorepo whose composer.json replaces 66
# packages with "self.version" while declaring no version and no
# extra.branch-alias (upstream symfony/symfony@8.1 is the same -- this probe is a
# faithful copy). In a bare scanner workspace composer cannot pin self.version, so
# the replaced symfony/console cannot satisfy doctrine/orm ^3.4's
# ^5.4||^6.0||^7.0, and resolution dies:
#
#   Your requirements could not be resolved to an installable set of packages.
#   php.runPreStep = true, but the pre-step failed
#   Could not find composer.lock file in /tmp/mend-scm/qa-fork-...-symfony
#   PhpDependencyResolver - resolveDependencies - END - tree size: 0
#
# Upstream ships no composer.lock either, so there is nothing to fall back to and
# the php tree ends empty (partialScanError=php, 6 direct / 0 transitive -- only
# the html/archive artifacts survive).
#
# The classic envs return the 21 composer packages from this same lockless repo,
# i.e. they never attempt the pre-step and parse composer.json directly. Turning
# the pre-step off puts DP on that same path.
php.runPreStep=false
